---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container  from "@nl06/design-system/components/Container.astro";
import Prose      from "@nl06/design-system/components/Prose.astro";

// Sample copy — drawn from project context. Edit at will.
const updated = "21 May 2026";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Now — nl06"
  description="What I'm working on this month."
  pathname="/now"
>
  <Container size="prose" class="now">
    <p class="dateline">Updated {updated}</p>
    <h1>Now</h1>
    <p class="sub">Following <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" rel="noopener">Derek Sivers' /now convention</a> — what's actively loaded into the next few months.</p>

    <Prose>
      <h2>Building</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The SPC India Member Residency application, due in June. The artifacts it leans on are this site and the ground station.</li>
        <li>Getting the Lucknow ground station to run unattended through the monsoon. Currently the chain stays cold between captures and the SatDump pipeline is touchy on resume.</li>
        <li>Three consequence chains in active resolution — they're tracked at <a href="https://chains.nl06.com">chains.</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Thinking about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Whether a one-rooftop install in Lucknow can produce useful independent PNT cross-checks without a second ground station to disambiguate local interference.</li>
        <li>How much of consequence-chain reasoning actually generalises — methodology or just a heuristic I happen to find useful.</li>
        <li>The right scope of the first hardware-software bet for the new venture. Two candidates, both space-adjacent. Killing one this month.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reading</h2>
      <p>Currently: <em>Working in Public</em> (Eghbal), <em>Seeing Like a State</em> (Scott), and a clutch of papers on rooftop LRIT site diversity. Notes land at <a href="https://reading.nl06.com">reading.</a> when they shift something.</p>
    </Prose>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .now { padding-top: var(--space-12); padding-bottom: var(--space-12); }
  .dateline {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--type-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-meta);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }
  .now > h1 { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .now > .sub {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--type-h4);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
  .now > :global(.prose-flow) { margin-top: var(--space-10); }
</style>
